--   Round-six lemma `T0n_eq`
-- statement:
--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFLMath`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFL.T0n_eq {K : ℕ} (hK : 1 ≤ K) (ρ : ℕ) (x y : ℕ) :
--       ∀ n, T0n K ρ n x y = ((y ^^^ (x &&& selM K ρ n) : ℕ) : ℤ)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** KFL §2: Lemma 13 on chunk triples (canonical layout `x, y, z` = slots `0, 1, 2`)
--
--   * `selM K ρ n = Σ_{i<n} 2^{ρ+iK}` (the selected-position mask), `testBit_selM`.
--   * `T0y_eq`: the ideal map `T0` of `ButterflyPacked` is `y ↦ y ⊕ (x ∧ selM (f-1))`;
--     `guardN_xor`: it preserves every guard.
--   * The pull maps of the eight lines as triple maps `lineP` (realised by `rot2`, after a slot
--     swap for the `y`-lines), their composite `FSc = lineP l₁ ∘ … ∘ lineP l₈` and the forward
--     `S0c`; `S0c_FSc`, `FSc_S0c` (inverse bijections), `FSc_good` (off the guard set `FSc = T0c`).
--   * The correction: `keyc = T0c ∘ FSc`; `bad_keyc` (bad to bad), `keyc_S0c` (onto the bad set),
--     `T0c_keyc` (the corrected pull is `T0c`).
--   * `T0c_XLc`: with the last selected bit (`flip1`) the composite is the row addition `RAc`.
--
